  "name": "Warbird",
  "description": "A single-seat WWII propeller fighter (a P-51D Mustang's numbers) on tricycle gear: fast, climbs hard, rolls quickly, and stalls sharply if pulled too slow.",
  "comment": "A vehicle preset (#379): see sedan.json for the format and plane.json for the aircraft block. A North American P-51D Mustang on the flight port's fighter airframe: 4,360 kg at take-off with a 75 kg pilot (the preset is 4,285; NAA report NA-46-130), a 21.8 m^2 wing of span 11.28 m (aspect ratio 5.8), one 1,111 kW (1,490 hp, military power) engine on a 3.4 m propeller whose push falls off as power / speed (engines.power), static thrust tuned to its 317 m take-off roll. Its wing's peak lift 1.7 at 16 degrees gives the ~100 mph clean stall; the tail stalls 5 degrees later than the wing, so a stall drops the nose. Ailerons tuned to about 90 degrees a second (NACA Report 868's P-51B peaks near 95). The air-speed limit is a safety net above its ~168 m/s top speed. cruiseSpeed and cruiseThrottle are the trim schema/validate.py and FMantleChassisDerive solve (FMantleFlightModel).",
  "movementType": "plane",
  "publishable": true,
